    "doc_text": "AFP_ENG_20061215.0091\n\nTOKYO, Dec 15 , 2006, 2006\n\nATTENTION - ADDS details ///\n\n\n\n\nJapan on Friday created a full-fledged defense ministry for the first time since World War II, when the United States stripped the defeated country of its right to a military.\n\nThe upper house voted by a majority, with support from the main opposition Democratic Party, to create the defense agency. The lower house had earlier passed the bill, meaning it becomes law, a parliamentary official said.\n\nPost-war Japan has had a \"Defense Agency\" with lower standing than full-fledged ministries as the 1947 constitution declared the country to be pacifist.\n\nDespite calling its troops the \"Self-Defense Forces\", Japan has one of the world's biggest military budgets at 4.81 trillion yen (41.6 billion dollars) a year.",
